---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import CTA from '../components/CTA.astro';
---
<Base title="Becoming a Government Contractor | Tidewater" description="A starting point for service operators considering government work. Understand the opportunity, gather your business information and check your bid readiness.">
<section class="section"><div class="container alt-hero"><p class="eyebrow">Getting started</p><h1>Becoming a government contractor.</h1><p class="lead">Start with the work your business can deliver. Then look at what a particular agency needs and what its solicitation requires.</p><a class="button" href="/contact">Talk to Tidewater <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></section>
<section class="section"><div class="container"><div class="section-head"><p class="eyebrow">Before your first bid</p><h2>Build a clear picture of your business.</h2><p>Requirements vary by agency and contract. These are starting points for a conversation, not a universal eligibility checklist.</p></div><div class="grid-3"><div class="panel"><h3>The work you can deliver</h3><p>Define your services, service area, staffing capacity and availability. Gather examples and references from work you have actually completed.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>Your business information</h3><p>Bring together your business registrations, relevant licenses and insurance details. Compare them with the requirements of the specific opportunity.</p></div><div class="panel"><h3>The agency's instructions</h3><p>Review the official notice, deadline, required documents and any updates. Check the agency's vendor-registration and submission process before preparing a response.</p></div></div></div></section>
<section class="section reverse"><div class="container grid-2"><div><p class="eyebrow">An optional starting point</p><h2>Check your bid readiness.</h2><p class="lead">Eleven questions to help identify the gaps.</p></div><div><p>Our free check covers business information, coverage, capacity and registrations. You get an illustrative score and a list of things to review. It is not an agency certification or a prediction of an award.</p><a class="button" href="/readiness">Take the readiness check <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div></div></section>
<CTA title="You can start with a question." body="You do not need to complete a quiz before getting in touch. Tell us about your business and the government work you are considering." />
</Base>
